  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan leaves Fairy Li Shan’s immortal aperture midway through the visit to Heavenly Lord Bai Zu and greets Qin Bai Sheng as Sha Huang. He offers a large transaction of Gu Immortals’ blessed lands for the coming auction and says he is only running an errand. Qin Bai Sheng accepts him into the sale and soon calls him Brother Sha.",
      "chapters": [
        736
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_fairy_li_shan",
        "char_heavenly_lord_bai_zu",
        "char_qin_bai_sheng",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Narration states Fang Yuan uses the fake name Sha Huang. Unfamiliar face turns his eight monstrous arms into ordinary zombie shoulders, shrinks his six meter body to a normal person’s build or shorter, and retracts his fangs so he looks weak rather than ruthless. He must hide from Northern Plains attention after Eighty-Eight True Yang Building, because Ma Hong Yun and Zhao Lian Yun are with Qin Bai Sheng and because Hei Lou Lan, Tai Bai Yun Sheng, and the eight arm heavenly zombie form cannot appear openly.",
      "chapters": [
        737
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "disguise-and-entry",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_northern_plains",
        "house_eighty_eight_true_yang_building",
        "char_ma_hong_yun",
        "char_zhao_lian_yun",
        "char_hei_lou_lan",
        "char_tai_bai_yun_sheng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At Dark Flow Giant City he enters the Northern Plains Zombie Alliance discussion hall, greets the hall as Sha Huang, and is questioned by Dragon Commander Ye Cha on whether the name is real. He answers that Sha Huang is the name he gave himself on the second day after becoming an immortal zombie, to mark a new beginning until he regains a living body. Huang Quan Weng accepts him as a Northern Plains Gu Immortal because he opened the door that even Yao Huang failed to push open.",
      "chapters": [
        740
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "zombie-alliance-membership",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_dark_flow_giant_city",
        "fac_zombie_alliance",
        "char_dragon_commander_ye_cha",
        "char_huang_quan_weng",
        "char_yao_huang"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At the auction Qin Bai Sheng judges that immortal zombie Sha Huang looks ordinary yet may have a rank eight refinement expert behind him, and that Fairy Li Shan would not otherwise stay close to a mere rank six immortal zombie.",
      "chapters": [
        753
      ],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "auction-reputation",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "After the auction Feng Jiu Ge presses Qin Bai Sheng for the seller. Qin Bai Sheng names Sha Huang as an immortal zombie. Feng Jiu Ge splits his force so one group can go to Northern Plains Zombie Alliance and seek Sha Huang there.",
      "chapters": [
        768
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "exposure",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_feng_jiu_ge"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fairy Li Shan later warns Fang Yuan that someone is investigating Sha Huang’s identity inside the alliance. Feng Jiu Ge reads the cover as a Northern Plains-tied immortal zombie who disguised himself and has major backing, possibly linked to Eighty-Eight True Yang Building’s collapse.",
      "chapters": [
        772
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "exposure",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
